    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Moovingo is delighted to present this superb mid-terrace home to the market, a beautifully maintained and upgraded property offering bright, well-proportioned accommodation in a highly sought-after Dún Laoghaire setting. Extended to the rear and with an attic conversion also, the house measures approx. 88 Sq.M excluding the converted attic space (14 Sq.M). A particular feature of the house is its directly south-facing orientation to the rear, with both the main living area and principal bedroom benefiting from excellent natural light throughout the day. The ground floor is finished with solid walnut flooring, which continues through the stairs and landing, while the kitchen was upgraded in 2025.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are two well-proportioned bedrooms, both with built-in wardrobes, alongside a fully renovated family bathroom completed in 2026. The principal bedroom enjoys a particularly impressive south-facing aspect and opens directly onto a private terrace which is quite the sun trap. A converted attic provides valuable additional accommodation, offering excellent flexibility for a variety of uses.\r\n\r\nTo the rear is a private and mature south-facing garden, designed for low-maintenance enjoyment and benefiting from convenient side access to the rear lane. The property has also undergone a number of important energy-efficiency upgrades, including triple-glazed windows to the front, upgraded rear glazing and insulation, and a Viessmann gas combi boiler installed in 2021. These improvements have contributed to an impressive B3 BER rating, making it eligible for Green Mortgages.\r\n\r\nArea Info\r\n\r\n39 Cross Avenue is ideally located within walking distance to Dun Laoghaire Main Street and Dun Laoghaire Shopping Centre and boasts a range of excellent local amenities, including shops, cafes and restaurants. The beautiful villages of Monkstown and Glasthule are both also within easy reach. There are a great selection of schools in the vicinity in addition to multiple childcare facilities. Recreational amenities include idyllic walks down Dun Laoghaire Pier as well as Sunday Strolls in People's Park which have a play area for kids and enjoys Sunday Markets with global foods. The road itself is a one-way road with limited passing traffic.\r\n\r\nThe area is well-serviced with excellent transport links including the Dun Laoghaire Dart Station which is within walking distance. Additionally, there are numerous Dublin Bus routes that serve the area and the M50 is also within easy reach."
      },
      {
